new file mode 100644
index 0000000..d6308d4
--- /dev/null
+++ b/renderer/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,38 @@
+# smallpt browser port
+
+The original renderer is by Kevin Beason: https://www.kevinbeason.com/smallpt/ .
+`smallpt-original.cpp` is the unmodified upstream source. The original MIT license
+is retained in `LICENSE.txt`. `public/images/cornell-reference.png` is the original
+render distributed with smallpt; it is shown while the browser renderer starts.
+
+`smallpt.cpp` retains the original camera, geometry, materials, 2×2 subpixel tent
+sampling, gamma conversion, and recursive Monte Carlo integrator. The port replaces
+the command-line/PPM entrypoint with `set_color` and `render_rows`, returning RGBA
+scanline buffers. A depth limit of 128 protects the WebAssembly stack. OpenMP is
+replaced by a dedicated browser module worker, requiring no cross-origin isolation
+headers or SharedArrayBuffer. The worker transfers four scanlines at a time to the
+canvas. Restarting terminates the previous worker so stale output cannot overwrite
+a new render.
+
+## Build
+
+Install Emscripten (`em++` must be on PATH), then run:
+
+```sh
+pnpm install --frozen-lockfile
+pnpm run build
+```
+
+`build` compiles the C++ source with Emscripten before the Astro production build.
+The compiled ES module and WebAssembly binary are also included in `public/wasm/`
+so the existing development workflow can consume them without a compiler.
+`pnpm run build:wasm` rebuilds only those artifacts.
+
+The prerendered homepage is written to `dist/client/index.html`. The app retains
+its configured `/devtools-times/` deployment base; all worker and asset URLs honor
+that base. Rendering, randomization, progress, image export, and reset run locally
+in the client. Changing quality or resolution restarts the current scene. Randomize
+changes both sphere tints and wall accents; Reset restores the upstream colors.
+
+The release build disables C++ exceptions and RTTI (neither is used), enables LTO,
+exports only the rendering/memory functions, and reserves a 1 MB execution stack.
